<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4679fcf0b91d088ad2fd4059a65232cb0de84ca9554817ec68c64a47feeb329</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T17:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd" /><summary type="html">About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says meeting between Putin and Zelensky at Miami G20 'impossible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1856e206fbcf10ebe1fb82aa21abc46da42d4ba30712a8642781773d307caccf</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said he was willing to meet Russian leader Vladimir Putin at the G20 summit in Miami for talks on ending the war. However, the Kremlin immediately ruled it out, saying it was "impossible" and that a meeting would only take place in Russian capital Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police suspect Normandy train derailment was result of sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:969ba2d71909c1e687c3e9abf8d573a6493783b1892107ca6645f4813f9517f0</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:48:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment--ddcadeb5d26c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment" /><summary type="html">A police source said Saturday that French investigators suspect sabotage caused a train derailment in northwest France after a fragment of rail was found on the track. At least 44 people were injured in the derailment that occurred a day earlier, including an 18-year-old woman "in a critical condition".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says unified Ireland ‘would be fantastic' during Dublin trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd97d7c8f9fd778b257305ff87b350f04a2c6f25d172eabd55fbe401ad4ca08f</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:51:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament--fbbff38c8ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said a unified Ireland would be “fantastic" during a weekend visit to a major tournament at his Irish golf course. The two-day trip to Ireland is the latest example of how the US leader blends his official duties with his personal interests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion poised for emotional comeback concert in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3dd029cde0b8db40babbbb83e500c119d9bb226646fb3fbf5620812f67cd06</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:23:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris--d2f545b260c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion is set to return to the stage in Paris on Saturday for her first full concert in six years, capping a years-long battle with a rare autoimmune disorder and marking a major milestone in the Canadian superstar’s comeback.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Battle over 'pervert' AI glasses in Europe's line of sight after scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f408c0b76076ce88f15dca78f8000300d3d6cedcf15a4405343ff4e99492f981</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-battle-over-pervert-ai-glasses-in-europe-s-line-of-sight-after-scandal" /><summary type="html">A scandal involving girls and women filmed secretly by "pervert"  AI glasses has sparked growing concern over this emerging technology – with a petition in Britain demanding a ban on their sale. Anyone wearing smart glasses can take photos, film videos or interact with an AI assistant, with sales now hitting the millions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges Trump to impose new Russia sanctions 'now', after deadly Ukraine strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b730cafe46122649c3434b6306e428a00d1232403cbc642267625414c6334548</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T19:13:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes--228fa885e3a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged US President Donald Trump to impose new sanctions on Russia over deadly strikes on Ukraine, as Kyiv and Moscow step up attacks and US-led efforts to end the war remain deadlocked.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Elections in Russia: the 1001 tricks to remove inconvenient candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be59a7e4589f25b7968f47a5e761078ffd385c9973dd160002f0aae43bdbb542</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T16:11:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates--c49abd54b7c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates" /><summary type="html">The Russian authorities are using dubious claims to disqualify candidates previously cleared to run in the parliamentary election from September 18 to 20. The war in Ukraine is making the Kremlin even more cautious about who is allowed to campaign.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>I'm extremely worried by extremists that win elections in Europe: Luxembourg's PM Luc Frieden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:879b824464caac2d3900cc5373773baf1a7e7baee552c8e65435417a548649e7</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:53:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260911-i-m-extremely-worried-by-extremists-that-win-elections-in-europe-luxembourg-s-pm-luc-friede--96d71fcdb103.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260911-i-m-extremely-worried-by-extremists-that-win-elections-in-europe-luxembourg-s-pm-luc-frieden" /><summary type="html">"European strategic autonomy" is a buzz phrase in Brussels and in EU capitals these days. What does it mean for space policy? That was one of the central points that we raised with the Prime Minister of Luxembourg, Luc Frieden, during his visit to Paris for the International Space Summit hosted by the French government on September 9 and 10. Major American aerospace companies were noticeably absent from the summit while the feud between Brussels and the Trump administration continues.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>A fire destroys part of a migrant camp in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f0ffb094e47d6cabca8612ae9af4d416cf7549446bc1df684e2e2203b8159d6</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-a-fire-destroys-part-of-a-migrant-camp-in-the-spanish-enclave-of-ceuta--b8e12cf63ee7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-a-fire-destroys-part-of-a-migrant-camp-in-the-spanish-enclave-of-ceuta" /><summary type="html">An apparently accidental fire destroyed about 40 shacks at a migrant camp in Ceuta, local media reported, but caused no injuries, Spanish police told AFP on Friday. The North African enclave saw tens of thousands of migrants arrive from Morocco in late July.</summary></entry><entry><title>French far-right leader polling ahead for 2027 election: should the EU be afraid?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:723607d74ec9812085fcdf3e8e5d00801ad56b27b0a000142410c09967676dcb</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:14:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-leader-polling-ahead-for-2027-election-should-the-eu-be-afraid--714a1da24d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-leader-polling-ahead-for-2027-election-should-the-eu-be-afraid" /><summary type="html">In Brussels, opinion polls coming out of France have not escaped attention. Two polls see far right leader Marine Le Pen beating all her likely rivals in the French presidential election, which is set to take place in April and May of next year.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Did the War on Terror succeed? Or did Washington fall into al Qaeda’s trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ea64f77f1d540da5df65fa19c5d9a2e5a4de2c18d3d0e9eb1fea8df2e8af638</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap--52617987fc7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW: Friday, September 11– 25 years on from 9/11, the international press reflects on the war on terror, its legacy and its failings. In France, the far-right National Rally party tries desperately to distance itself from the overtly racist comments of one of its security officials, made while on duty for his day job as a police officer. Finally, a fossilised feather may give us new insights into why birds survived the asteroid that killed the dinosaurs.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's Emma Bonino, champion of battles to legalise abortion and divorce, dies at 78</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b971e17a4ea6be702cfb84ac18e92991e758104a5e7a6febe5df9302d75c90b</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-italy-s-emma-bonino-champion-of-battles-to-legalise-abortion-and-divorce-dies-at-78--08dac3031ddb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-italy-s-emma-bonino-champion-of-battles-to-legalise-abortion-and-divorce-dies-at-78" /><summary type="html">Veteran feminist activist Emma Bonino, who rose to political prominence in the 1970s as a leader of campaigns to legalise abortion and divorce in heavily Roman Catholic Italy over the objections of the Vatican, has died aged 78. Bonino, who was diagnosed with lung cancer in 2015, served as foreign minister and European commissioner but failed in her bid to become Italy's first woman president.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f88130f0700fb3f2f8483ac06dd4ce28e20ba5b2c7c1ad8cbe10f82098f14</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:03:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications--25ea30849574.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications" /><summary type="html">From communications to crewed spaceflight, French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place in the space race on Thursday – notably, against the United States and China. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".</summary></entry><entry><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:099e45b9a4c448b5730caf2e2aa166d45a5ee5c3ad0db87b6568267f561a88e9</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush--ae85c7241bed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Space Summit: Europe plays catch-up with US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:684ec64e4f87b848d1e0ffbdbdbcb947269a73efd4784bda9c782a94fcaa4e55</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:28:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china--975a45d2435a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china" /><summary type="html">The space sector is booming. The global industry expected to reach a value of €2 trillion mark by 2040. But behind this spectacular growth lies major geopolitical challenges, particularly for Europe. In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Charles Pellegrin speaks to Kai-Uwe Schrogl at the International Space Summit in Paris. Schrogl, a political affairs adviser to the European Space Agency, answers questions about the future of the great beyond and Europe’s place in the new space race.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Russia tricks 'vulnerable' foreigners to fight in Ukraine war, Amnesty reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:050747628114ceb3d783c958b6a48174eae0bc095046525cbc46652a48e960f6</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-russia-tricks-vulnerable-foreigners-to-fight-in-ukraine-war-amnesty-reports--21a0ba2cee79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-russia-tricks-vulnerable-foreigners-to-fight-in-ukraine-war-amnesty-reports" /><summary type="html">Foreign nationals are being tricked into fighting for the Russian army against Ukraine through fake job offers, an Amnesty International report said Thursday, citing interviews with prisoners of war. The average targeted recruit is under 40, living in a poorer country and lured by the "promise of a job", Amnesty's secretary-general said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Revisited: Consequences of the 2022 Nord Stream pipeline sabotage are still being felt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09e809b2135d9dc45d2641d62272a78e6bdb179522973f32b1b0da1d724263cb</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:07:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260910-revisited-consequences-of-the-2022-nord-stream-pipeline-sabotage-are-still-being-felt--9c31cb3af302.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260910-revisited-consequences-of-the-2022-nord-stream-pipeline-sabotage-are-still-being-felt" /><summary type="html">It is one of the most spectacular acts of sabotage committed since World War II. On the night of September 26, 2022, three of the four pipes of the Nord Stream 1 and Nord Stream 2 gas pipelines exploded on the seabed of the Baltic Sea. 465 thousand metric tons of methane were released into the atmosphere. The long-standing and strategic link between Russia and Germany severed for good.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>RN 'breach': Amid 'severe' differences with 'bright, young' Bardella, Le Pen 'dictates party line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:489035c117474a338aaaa69d5529b800ff6cf3788bc8d69871132bfa3019993a</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T12:25:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rn-breach-amid-severe-differences-with-bright-young-bardella-le-pen-dictates-party-line-1--39a881e6ef18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rn-breach-amid-severe-differences-with-bright-young-bardella-le-pen-dictates-party-line-1" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Mallet, Financial Times Senior Editor at the World News Desk. He interprets the emerging tensions between Marine Le Pen and Jordan Bardella as more than a clash of personalities. They reveal a deeper struggle over the political future of France's far-right National Rally is becoming as they find themselves in prime position in their hunt to capture the French presidency. Bardella is formally president of the party and has developed his own political constituency, particularly among younger voters and parts of the business community. Yet Mallet argues that Le Pen continues to exercise the decisive ideological and strategic authority.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bayeux Tapestry 'mania' sweeps UK as first exhibition outside France opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1dfe9e5e8ecbf6fd9f463d5813f131e6118be58c6b0d23ae837d85887572e69</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:05:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-bayeux-tapestry-mania-sweeps-uk-as-first-exhibition-outside-france-opens--9986e6fe38f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-bayeux-tapestry-mania-sweeps-uk-as-first-exhibition-outside-france-opens" /><summary type="html">The British Museum on Thursday opened its doors for the first public display of the 1,000-year-old Bayeux Tapestry outside of France. The museum has so far sold a record-breaking 100,000 tickets to see the tapestry, which depicts the Norman conquest of England under William the Conqueror.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Passengers or pilots?' Europe looks to challenge US dominance in space sector with €10 billion plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62f9e5327c5692e88520154317b9976ab8c492c6a3a644bb7577dde9aa38292c</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:56:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-passengers-or-pilots-europe-looks-to-challenge-us-dominance-in-space-sector-with-_10-billio--9d31a0c4aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-passengers-or-pilots-europe-looks-to-challenge-us-dominance-in-space-sector-with-%E2%82%AC10-billion-plan" /><summary type="html">Key figures from Europe’s space industry and other international players have converged on Paris to discuss how to advance the continent’s ambitions in a global market dominated by the United States.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU gives Spain 115 mn euros aid over Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee0e2ee7c85af5dc09b0b403eb5589e60f382346106b5168b4833d3347533a54</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:06:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis--38a16ccc97da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">The EU on Wednesday said it was granting Spain 115 million euros ($130 million) in emergency aid to help bolster border security and assist returns after the massive migrant rush into the north African exclave. More than 70,000 migrants crossed into Spanish territory from Morocco on July 30 and 31 in an unprecedented rush that left scores dead, most by drowning as they tried to swim around a breakwater. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rungis market chief on supply chains and feeding the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24924d92dee35f152a4c28ea6bdd9c8cf23ab22ff1a7b0ad122abcea4778abb5</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:05:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world--b449a157d7e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world" /><summary type="html">In today’s edition, FRANCE 24’s Delano D'Souza speaks with the man at the heart of France's food supply chain. Stéphane Layani is the head of the Rungis wholesale food market – the largest of its kind in Europe – and chairman of the World Union of Wholesale Markets. Earlier this year Layani came out with a book titled Le Monde a faim, or "The World is Hungry" in English. In his interview, he gives his perspective on how France's food system will transform in the coming years.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic calls snap elections after nearly two years of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:131e1dba88cd207dd3df59bc8b07c5075916af63e02dc9354984f871a6b9b9f2</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:15:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests--5f70b882a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic on Wednesday called snap parliamentary elections for October 25. They are expected to be a key test of his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strike near Ukraine-Moldova border kills at least two as Ukraine targets oil terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f22ea4d2c5c03f136a6cee9ed5d87df1ed5cdeef2773e875177b43e08b54d8</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:51:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-ter--fc9e4da4f8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-terminal" /><summary type="html">An overnight Russian drone strike at a border crossing between Ukraine and Moldova killed at least two people, Odesa's regional governor said Wednesday. Moldovan Prime Minister Vasile Tofan said that 17 drones had hit Moldovan territory in August alone as both Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on military and energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Travellers in UK face ongoing disruption after air traffic control glitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea87a311684be06e5847f22d8c7d77e73df4354b0481dfb360dfb37dde22f06e</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T03:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch--92d15f16fe8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch" /><summary type="html">Flights from British airports began to resume Wednesday after a glitch in the country's air traffic control service left hundreds of thousands of passengers stranded and 2,000 cancellations, costing airlines millions of pounds. Authorities warned that travellers would continue to experience delays as airlines scrambled to recover from the outage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump tells Putin he wants swift end to Ukraine war, Kremlin says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5482155f45e4756fa3f9f910356a4e6c8abfb54489ed50fd9279135745862d8</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:07:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says--5f2aae4d01c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told Russian President Vladimir Putin he wanted a swift end to the Ukraine war, the Kremlin said, arguing that peace could pave the way for a broad restoration of US-Russia ties. The hour-long call Tuesday followed weekend talks by US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Moscow and Kyiv to try to revive stalled peace efforts.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Missiles or mediation? Trump envoys shuttle between Russia and Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ff7f8fd047f69f7506923c7bbf86ed43ff86b8a15634b83b0803399c715550f</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine--b5fc503da412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s momentum on the battlefield was a primary focus at July’s NATO summit in Turkey. Kyiv’s long-range drones and US President Donald Trump’s surprise announcement that the Washington would allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles on in the country. However, Trump's deal has yet to materialize. Moreover, Russia has ramped up cruise missile launches and Ukraine has run out of air defenses to stop them. Moscow is also failing to stop incoming missiles. In today’s edition we ask: What happens in war when offense proves better than defense for both sides?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cbfcaefa8594cdfb9af054c6a563a44f8fc960ee05cc2ca3c441709cb494b3e</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower reopens after row over limits on women staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1b2dd5b015f4fba0c96454c364ec33b721429364f72ff8e942560ef1e17d4a5</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:18:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff--477be6cb13b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff" /><summary type="html">The Eiffel Tower reopened Tuesday, a day after one of the world's most-visited landmarks was closed by a strike to protest what a union official called "unacceptable" management instructions limiting the presence of women during a visit by a Hindu religious group close to Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s ruling nationalist party.</summary></entry></feed>
